/ Authoring UI for the structured question types. question_builder_controller renders the editor
/ client-side from the hidden config field and re-serialises on every edit, so a normal submit
/ carries question[config] as JSON (parsed onto the jsonb column by QuestionsController#parsed_config).
.tjs-builder data-controller='question-builder' data-question-builder-type-value=@question.question_type
  = f.hidden_field :config, value: @question.config.to_json, data: { 'question-builder-target': 'config' }
  .tjs-builder__editor data-question-builder-target='editor' data-action='input->question-builder#serialize change->question-builder#serialize'
  - if @question.drag_drop?
    .tjs-builder__help
      h3.tjs-builder__help-title How to build a drag-and-drop question
      ol
        li In the Question Text box above, write the sentence and mark each blank with {{1}}, {{2}}, {{3}} and so on — these become the drop zones students fill in.
        li Add one item per draggable tile. The item's text is what the student sees on the tile.
        li
          | For an item that answers a blank, put that blank's number in the
          strong  Blank #(s)
          | field (e.g. 1 for the first blank).
        li
          | An item can answer more than one blank — list the numbers separated by commas (e.g.
          strong  1,3
          | ). Students can reuse the same tile in each of those blanks.
        li
          | A blank can also have more than one correct item — put that blank's number on each item that should be accepted, and any of them placed in the blank scores it.
        li
          | Leave the
          strong  Blank #(s)
          | field empty to make an item a distractor — a wrong option that isn't the answer to any blank.
        li Every blank must have an item assigned to it before the question can be saved.
      p.tjs-builder__help-note Example: “The CPU has a {{1}} unit and a {{2}} unit.” with items “control” (Blank 1), “arithmetic logic” (Blank 2) and “storage” (no blank — a distractor).
  - if @question.fill_blank?
    .tjs-builder__help
      h3.tjs-builder__help-title How to build a gap-fill question
      ol
        li In the Question Text box above, write the sentence and mark each blank with {{1}}, {{2}}, {{3}} and so on — students type the missing word into each one.
        li Add one row per blank. Put the blank's number in the Blank # field and the word students must type in the Accepted answer(s) field.
        li
          | To accept more than one wording for a blank, separate the alternatives with a vertical bar (e.g.
          strong  RAM|random access memory
          | ). Matching ignores capitals and surrounding spaces.
        li Every blank must have at least one accepted answer before the question can be saved.
      p.tjs-builder__help-note Example: “A loop that runs a set number of times is a {{1}} loop.” with Blank 1 accepting “count-controlled|count controlled”.
  - if @question.ordering?
    .tjs-builder__help
      h3.tjs-builder__help-title How to build an ordering question
      ol
        li Use the Question Text box above for the instruction (e.g. “Put the steps of a bubble sort in order.”).
        li Add one item per step and write them in the correct order — top is first, bottom is last.
        li Use the ↑ / ↓ buttons to reorder items. Students see the items shuffled and rebuild this sequence.
        li You need at least two items. Each item placed in its correct position earns part of the marks.
      p.tjs-builder__help-note Example: items “Fetch”, “Decode”, “Execute” entered in that order.
  - if @question.classify?
    .tjs-builder__help
      h3.tjs-builder__help-title How to build a classify question
      ol
        li Use the Question Text box above for the instruction (e.g. “Drag each statement to the correct category.”).
        li Add at least two targets — these are the named buckets students will drag items into.
        li Add each item and use the dropdown to assign it to the correct target.
        li Every item must be assigned to a target before the question can be saved.
        li Students see the items shuffled and drag them into the matching buckets. Each correctly placed item earns part of the marks.
      p.tjs-builder__help-note Example: targets “Embedded system” and “General-purpose computer” with items like “Has a dedicated purpose” assigned to “Embedded system”.
